WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:02.810
It’s chaos on the streets.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:07.910
People are running as fast as they can as
monsters and horrors beyond imagination spill

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.179
out of every alleyway.

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:14.889
A monstrous, reptilian beast had a screaming
police man in its jaws.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:20.550
A strange statue was standing on top of a
pile of bodies, all with broken necks, and

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.720
a horde of flesh-eating zombies chased some
terrified civilians into broken storefronts.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.800
In short, all hell is breaking loose, and
you’re right there in the middle of it.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.430
As you try to avoid the legion of hungry undead,
you see a beautiful woman beckoning you into

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.430
an alley.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.289
You run to her, hoping that she’ll have
found some way out, but when you’re in there

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:46.860
and alone with her, desperately clutching
the one pocket knife you managed to grasp

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.899
in your trembling hand before your house was
overrun by flesh-eating insects, she begins

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:53.399
to laugh at you.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.980
The woman starts to change right before your
eyes - Her flowing red dress transforms into

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:05.220
impenetrable samurai armor, her features become
hard and severe, and a deathly sharp katana

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.979
begins to manifest in her hand.

00:01:07.979 --> 00:01:13.170
As the anomalous swordsman walks towards you
on this, the most terrifying day of your life,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.390
you realize that you probably won’t live
to see sundown.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:21.930
One of the most terrifying scenarios explored
in the archives of the SCP Foundation is that

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.870
of SCP-5000, events during which the Foundation's
primary directive changes from the study and

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:33.229
containment of anomalies, to the extinction
of all human life.

00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:38.770
What would you do, in the shoes of a Foundation
researcher during SCP-5000?

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.400
What anomalies would you use to kill people
or stop certain Groups of Interest from taking

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.110
down the foundation?

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:50.271
We posed this question to you, the viewers
of SCP Explained on our community tab, with

00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:56.040
one caveat: you can't use any nuclear weapons
or any anomalies that can totally destroy

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.460
the world quickly.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.310
So, without further ado, let's see what kind
of destruction you all wrought.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.950
LeoWorld said, "As a researcher, I would use
the radio to make people hear the words of

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:12.890
SCP-4511/the swine god to make them sacrifice
others to his burning insides.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.650
It’s good to let a less popular Scp have
some spotlight in this scenario.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.190
Perhaps this idea could also be used for some
groups of interests."

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:25.980
This response reminds me of something my grandma
used to say: If you have to wipe out the human

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.241
race in order to destroy a horrifying entity
lurking in the collective unconscious, you

00:02:30.241 --> 00:02:34.599
might as well get creative with it.

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:36.180
She was a strange lady.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.099
Anyway, all hail the swine god, may his eternal
flame cleanse the earth.

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:44.300
This particular strategy would probably take
a while to have an effect on the population

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.700
at large, but points for originality.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:53.040
Yissi Biiyte said, "I think a picture of 096
would make an excellent weapon against Groups

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.040
of Interest.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.930
Small, lightweight, discreet, guaranteed death
of the target."'

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.410
Now, this is a classic.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.569
If it ain't broke, don't fix it!

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.129
If you've got a killing machine ready to be
deployed as soon as someone looks at his face,

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:08.989
why not take advantage of that?

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:13.409
The only potential hangup is the problem of
getting the pictures to the Groups of Interest

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:15.599
without looking at them yourself.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:19.769
Once you've got a system down, then you can
just spread 096's picture around and watch

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:21.660
the body count rack up!

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.989
This strategy is a lot like playing Call of
Duty, it also destroys lives with a Headshot.

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:31.170
Derek McDaniel said, "SCP-2501.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.170
Think about it.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:36.610
A telekinetic claw that can crush potentially
anything while keeping a safe distance from

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:41.550
any threats is a perfect weapon for stealth,
hitting prior targets, and more."

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.489
No muss, no fuss, just a telekinetic claw.

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:46.849
Great thinking!

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:50.620
GhostOfTheCove said, "Okay, this is gonna
take a while:

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.620
1.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.920
Wake 239 up and tell her about the Chaos Insurgency.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.600
Show her videos of their raids on Foundation
Sites, basically do everything to make them

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.630
look like the "bad guys".

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:04.860
If all goes well, she'll wipe them from existence
like she did with the D-class.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.000
Rinse and repeat for any GOIs that come off
as hostile.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.000
2.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.990
Use SCP-038 to clone anomalies that can cause
death.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:19.100
For example, clone SCP-4955, find field agents
who specialize in melee combat, and send them

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.900
out into densely-populated areas.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:22.900
3.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:30.310
Blast recordings of SCPs 336, 661, and 2284's
voices on radio stations all over the world.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:36.130
Have 336's recordings be as long as possible,
get 661 to spread destructive thoughts over

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:43.160
and over on recording, and make 2284 state
that there's a safezone at SCP-2316, so that

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:46.550
people head over there and recognize the bodies
in the water.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.550
4.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:53.530
Airdrop SCP-469 into Delhi, India, which is
the world's noisiest city, according to Google.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:54.530
5.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.350
Using a front company, distribute pamphlets
full of instructions on how to survive the

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.350
event.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:03.570
On one of the pages of the pamphlets, print
the descriptions of several deadly infohazardous

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.930
SCPs (1128, 2316, etc).

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.020
6.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.900
Integrate SCP-3280 into the water cycle."

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.900
So this is the way the world goes out.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:20.720
Not with a bang, not with a whimper, but with
a fleet of gaslighting knives, potentially

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:26.100
deadly radio broadcasts, a city crushed by
a mass of wings, and killer anomalies disguised

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.620
as life-saving resources.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:33.340
And then the global water supply being slowly
replaced by sapient water that hates humans.

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:37.000
Is there a word for being impressed and terrified
at the same time?

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.669
Because if there is, you'll find my picture
next to it in the dictionary.

00:05:40.669 --> 00:05:46.270
Camille Lartaud-Balosso said, "To ensure all
children disappear, I would stop answering

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:49.100
SCP-3034, the Counting Station.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:53.539
No matter how well-hidden or protected some
kids will be, they should disappear eventually.

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:59.280
I'm also just really curious what would happen,
I find that SCP spooky and fascinating"

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.650
Well, that's absolutely terrifying.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:05.650
I can only imagine the chaos that would ensue
once the adults noticed that all of the children

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:07.300
in the world had vanished.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.520
You probably wouldn't even need anomalous
measures to take care of them.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:13.460
Their paranoia and rage would do the rest.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:17.979
This isn't the most efficient method, but
it's the one that feels the most like an unpublished

00:06:17.979 --> 00:06:21.250
Stephen King novel, so you've got that going
for you.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:26.870
Cheat Code Master said, "I always keep a half-inch
model of the original generation one Devastator

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.750
from Transformers in my pocket.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:34.550
I could put SCP-914 on the very fine setting
go into the input, hold my half inch Devastator

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:38.780
in the palm of my hand, as the door closes
shout "Prepare to meet your doom!

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:43.840
Nothing can withstand the might of Devastator!",
and then I'll personally unleash my full destructive

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.520
potential as the 120-meter tall combiner (It's
officially documented in transformers lore

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.690
that through Mass Displacement Technology
Combiners not only become bigger than the

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:56.789
sum of their parts, but Godzilla sized)."

00:06:56.789 --> 00:07:01.460
Before we get into the plan itself...you always
keep a half-inch model of the original generation

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:04.570
one Devastator from Transformers in your pocket?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:06.379
Just want to make sure I heard that right.

00:07:06.379 --> 00:07:09.259
No judgment, clearly you have a good reason.

00:07:09.259 --> 00:07:13.280
And that reason is that one day, you'll be
able to use the Clockworks to transform yourself

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:19.050
into a 120-meter-tall Devastator and obliterate
all of humanity in the most ambitious crossover

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.150
event of all time.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:25.750
Legendary Hydreigon said, "I would use the
nerfing gun in order to use it on the groups

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.860
of interest to devolve them into cavemen,
but also against the people we're trying to

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:34.710
kill as well, then let them kill each other
in territorial struggles, while they also

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.150
wouldn't be aware of attacks by the other
scps that have been released, making wiping

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:45.370
out humanity faster and much more easier to
get done before scp 5000 could do their reset

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.370
button"

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:50.630
I had no idea we had so many supervillains
in the SCP Explained audience!

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:55.020
Using the Nerfing Gun to Nerf all of humanity,
that's truly on another level.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:59.770
Release SCP-682 into the fray, and things
will get downright prehistoric.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:05.160
Nevermore Ghoul said, "As a researcher, I
suggest you Unleashing scp 053, the little

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:10.660
girl, into any large survival bunkers/communities
that enemy organizations have created to save

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:11.960
humanity.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:16.120
Easy to sneak her in and cause a mass amount
of death due to her abilities.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.789
As to how to get her co-operation in killing
all life promise her more play time with scp

00:08:20.789 --> 00:08:21.789
682."

00:08:21.789 --> 00:08:25.520
Okay, seriously, these are getting downright
diabolical!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.180
Since the Young Girl seems to be unaware of
her effect on people, you probably wouldn't

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.860
have to promise her anything.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.640
In fact, maybe it's best that she doesn't
know she's being used as a pawn in a plan

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.969
to wipe out all of humankind.

00:08:36.969 --> 00:08:40.370
Why pile on extra trauma during the apocalypse,
right?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:45.490
Silver Kuroma said, "Well, I have been a fan
of SCP for years now, so here is what I would

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.490
do:

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:47.490
1.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:50.680
Get a hold of SCP-079 or the Self Learning
Computer

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.680
2.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:54.470
Put it on a little cart that was used to roll
in the TV on school

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:55.620
3.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.800
Go to SCP-682’s containment sight
4.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:04.110
Struck a deal with it, since I know that SCP-079
and SCP-682 have a form of friendship then

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.500
it could work
5.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:11.220
If the deal fails, then get SCP-999 to hug
him until he becomes way less hostile and

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:15.329
agrees to help us, the deal being that if
he does help us, then he will be allowed to

00:09:15.329 --> 00:09:20.610
leave the facility to a more open area in
a certain range, and he will get a few Class-D

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.520
personnel as playthings
6.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:28.339
Get the assistance of SCP-343 to help us get
rid of the menace and rebuild the world a

00:09:28.339 --> 00:09:29.750
bit easier
7.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:35.151
Get the brilliance of the smartest SCP’s
out there, one of them being SCP-049, since

00:09:35.151 --> 00:09:37.570
this could be the pestilence he wanted to
eradicate

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.690
8.

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:44.430
Let the world know about the foundation and
help survivors and such, like this was a SCP-001

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.630
“When Day Breaks” scenario
9.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:50.680
Neutralize or terminate SCP-5000
10.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:51.950
Rebuild the world"

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.860
A bright spot of optimism in the darkness!

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:59.580
Not quite what the prompt was going for, but
it's admirable that you'd try to save humanity

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.460
somehow instead of just burning it all down.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.430
You might as well give it a shot, but be careful.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:09.310
If you're trying to save the world, the SCP
Foundation itself is going to be gunning for

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:13.550
you, and you'll be operating without the organization's
resources behind you.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.670
Good luck!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:19.610
Exi_M said, "Here’s an interesting one:
3008, the infinite IKEA.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.680
Make signs pointing to it that make it look
like a shelter, and disguise it as one.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:28.269
People run in, and they’re trapped forever
(or at least until they die to the employees)"

00:10:28.269 --> 00:10:33.110
So rather than destroying humanity directly,
you can just confine them to an endless purgatory

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.149
of Swedish meatballs and affordably-priced
furniture.

00:10:36.149 --> 00:10:39.690
Great way to get the job done while keeping
your hands technically clean.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:45.510
Vlask Gaming said, "I'd Use SCP-2000 with
a modification that would inject all the clones

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:51.600
with SCP-008 to create an endless never ending
horde of zombies to release into the world.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.680
if the site is never retaken and is allowed
to continue this process I could, in theory,

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:01.820
have a legit endless supply of SCP-008-1's
to swarm the world with."

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.360
The Walking Dead approach!

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:09.610
You've gotta give it up for the classics,
a good old zombie apocalypse with an SCP Foundation

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:10.610
twist.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:15.250
Always R.A said, "I suspect humanitarian aid
packages will be deployed by do-gooders at

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.260
some point.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:21.100
If so, slip in a set of SCP-178 into one of
the larger refuges.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:26.390
Since third parties caught up in a 178 incident
are also vulnerable to attack: job done.

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:30.460
And since any sufficiently large group of
people will have at least one goofball among

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:34.959
them, this could help wreck major trade routes
during the early days or weeks."

00:11:34.959 --> 00:11:38.910
I always had a feeling that the decline of
the human race would start with a pair of

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.370
3-D glasses.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.910
Everyone told me I was out of my mind, and
that I'd have to leave my showing of Avatar

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:45.520
The Way of Water without a refund.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:51.880
But look at me now, I was right all along.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:58.680
Kirby Kona said, "As a researcher in the scenario,
I'd find SCP-743, The deadly infinite Chocolate

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:05.130
Fountain, and place it in SCP-914, The Clockwerks,
on Either Fine or Very fine, if on Very fine

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:09.899
it’s still able to be moved and carried,
I'd take it to a refugee camp and wait...wait

00:12:09.899 --> 00:12:15.750
till the now improved creatures tear those
who are resisting the Foundation to shreds."

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.050
Death by chocolate!

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:21.010
Well, death by swarms of anomalous arthropods
emerging from a chocolate fountain, but that

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.570
just doesn't sound as good.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.140
Either way, that's a sweet victory.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:31.060
Johnrie18 said, "So, if the goal as I understand
it is to wipe out the entire human race WITHOUT

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:36.019
using reality-warping SCPs of any kind, there
are a number of options to choose from.

00:12:36.019 --> 00:12:41.740
First, I'd start with SCP 2419 and let loose
the thousands of unliving D-class who have

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.260
had every trace of humanity wiped from their
souls.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:48.829
They should be more than eager to wrack up
as high of a body count as possible.

00:12:48.829 --> 00:12:55.120
Then I'd use SCPs capable of targeting specific
areas or population centers like SCP-923,

00:12:55.120 --> 00:13:01.110
a satellite whose rays drive people into a
murderous rage, or SCP-2617, a Russian radio

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:05.990
tower that can summon an army of ice soldiers
to exterminate anything within a pre-programmed

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.019
set of coordinates.

00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:14.070
Also, while there is no shortage oF bloody-thirsty
SCPs out there, including SCP-082 aka Fernand

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:19.870
the Cannibal, or SCP-953, the Polymorphic
Humanoid, I'd start with a bigger gun.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:26.970
SCP-353 aka Vector, is a 26-year-old girl
with the ability to absorb, contain, manipulate

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:29.339
and release viruses as she pleases.

00:13:29.339 --> 00:13:33.320
She also happens to delight in killing as
many people as she can, so I have a feeling

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:38.310
she'd be more than happy to help, even against
other agencies out to combat the Foundation.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.800
I may have been thinking about this for a
while."

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.830
You don't say!

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:47.550
Thank you, Johnrie, for one of the most in-depth
and terrifying responses to our prompt.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:52.820
And on behalf of humanity, thank you for channeling
this energy into SCP-related pursuits instead

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:55.709
of bringing about the actual apocalypse.

00:13:55.709 --> 00:13:59.910
Between the laughing men, the rogue satellite,
the Russian radio tower, and Vector...humanity,

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:06.070
and the dark passenger that dwells deep within
every human psyche, doesn't stand a chance.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.519
Now go check out “SCP-5000 Why?

00:14:08.519 --> 00:14:14.799
- The Full Story Compilation” and “How
SCP-682 Tried to Stop SCP-5000” for more!

